## Feedforward constraints & Jidoka test gates

To prevent rework loops and maximize first-pass yield ($\ge 90\%$):

1. **Feedforward Context Assembly:** Before starting code generation, identify domain constraints, relevant historical defects from `evidence/rework.md`, and active role boundaries.
2. **Deterministic Pre-Flight Checks:** Run local tests and mechanical gates (`{{TEST_COMMAND}}`) incrementally after every discrete file modification rather than waiting until turn completion.
3. **Automated Stop-on-Defect (Jidoka / Autonomation):** If any mechanical gate or unit test fails, halt new feature generation immediately, isolate root cause, and resolve before proceeding. Do not build new code on top of a failing test.

